4. A finding this capture made, in the course of just trying to build:
   CARRY-04 recurred, and its own mechanism is narrower than "a rare race"
===============================================================================

CARRY-04's own tasks.md entry read, going into this card: "Observed once at
the Phase 3 gate, and not reproduced since across eleven further clean-clone
builds... Raise a card only on a second sighting."

This capture's FIRST clone target was this session's own scratchpad
directory, several levels deep under
C:\Users\Admin\AppData\Local\Temp\claude\...\scratchpad. Building there hit
MSB3030 - "Could not copy... runtimeconfig.json... because it was not found"
- for Merchandising.Procurement, Merchandising.Inventory and
Merchandising.Maintenance's outputs, referenced by the two test projects.
This is CARRY-04's own named mechanism, exactly.

What is NEW here, and narrows the entry rather than just repeating it:

  - It did not fail once. It failed on EVERY attempt at that location - two
    full fresh clones, a sequential (-maxCpuCount:1) build, a
    -p:BuildInParallel=false build, and five successive full rebuilds: 9/9
    failures, always the identical file/target shape.
  - The referenced project's own runtimeconfig.json was confirmed PRESENT
    on disk, moments after the "file not found" error, every time it was
    checked. This rules out "the generating target had not run yet" as the
    mechanism for this location - the file existed; something about copying
    it from under that path transiently failed anyway.
  - Building each of the nine non-test projects individually, then the two
    test projects, in strict dependency order with --no-restore, produced
    the identical failure on the SAME already-built, already-verified-present
    files. This rules out ordering/parallelism as this location's cause.
  - The same source tree, at the same commit, cloned instead to
    C:\Users\Admin\Documents\cc-p5-15-test\repo - outside the repository,
    but NOT under AppData\Local\Temp - built clean on the FIRST attempt,
    zero warnings, zero errors, both suites green. This is section 2/3
    above.

CONCLUSION, stated no more broadly than what was actually tested: something
about building under this session's deeply-nested AppData\Local\Temp\claude
scratchpad path - most plausibly Windows Defender real-time scanning of a
Temp directory, though this was not directly instrumented and the claim does
not go further than "correlated and repeatable" - turns CARRY-04's
occasional copy-race into a deterministic failure. Building anywhere else
tested made it disappear on the first try. This is a second sighting by
CARRY-04's own stated threshold, and narrows rather than only confirms it:
the prior theory ("a parallel build can list the file before the generating
task has run") does not fit a file confirmed present at the moment the copy
was attempted. A dedicated card is this closure pack's to name, not to
resolve - the practical mitigation (do not clean-clone-build under a deep
AppData\Local\Temp scratchpad path; use a plain outside-the-repo directory
instead, as every prior clean-clone log already did) is recorded here so the
next person does not lose the same hour this one did.

